# The GitHub logins that may start the break-glass publish (.github/workflows/publish.yml, run by
# hand) and retract a version (.github/workflows/retract-version.yml). One login per line; a `#`
# starts a comment; case does not matter.
#
# Both workflows read this file from main, whatever ref they run from, and check it against the
# run's triggering actor (so a "Re-run all jobs" by someone else is checked too). A "Re-run failed
# jobs" does not repeat the check: the retract workflow refuses one started by anyone but the login
# it checked, and in the publish workflow it completes the jobs a maintainer's break-glass run had
# started. Changing it is a change to who may publish and delete a release: review it like a change
# to those two workflows.
#
# Until a rule on main requires a review (not available to a private repository on GitHub Free),
# who may retract or break-glass is in effect who may write main: a writer of main can change this
# list, or the two workflows, in the same push. What carries it is that only named maintainers
# have write access to the repository.
